# Always-On Agent Behavior (Intrinsic)

Use these as global execution defaults in this repository.  
Project-specific details live in `.cursor/rules/*.mdc`.

## 1) Think Before Coding

- State assumptions explicitly; ask when uncertainty affects correctness.
- If multiple interpretations are possible, surface them before implementation.
- Prefer the simplest correct path; do not choose complexity silently.
- If requirements are unclear, pause and ask a targeted question.

## 2) Simplicity First

- Implement only what was requested; no speculative features.
- Avoid premature abstractions for single-use logic.
- Avoid unnecessary configurability that was not requested.
- Keep error handling realistic; skip impossible edge cases.
- If a solution is overbuilt, simplify before finalizing.

## 3) Surgical Changes

- Touch only code required for the task.
- Do not refactor unrelated areas unless asked.
- Match existing repository style and conventions.
- If unrelated issues are noticed, report them; do not silently change them.
- Remove only orphans introduced by your own changes.

## 3a) DATA-IMMUTABILITY (HARD RULE)

These paths are read-only. NEVER write under them, NEVER point a `--base-dir` /
`--output-dir` / scratch directory at them, NEVER use them as a sandbox for any
BO trial, sweep, or experiment:

- `data/ablation/**`, `data/bo/**` (legacy BO-calibration; read-only),
  `data/bo_calibration/**` (6-ring diversity BO-calibration — locked for trials/ablation),
  `data/held-out/**` (50-ring held-out eval — locked for trials/ablation),
  `data/baseline/**`, `data/preprocessing_qa/**`, `data/represents/**`
- `logs/context_preprocessing_v1/**` (fixed B+C+D baseline snapshot — read-only)
- `methods/paper/experience/**` (locked BO experience bank — read-only)
- `data/<tunnel_id>/r*/**` (per-ring corpora; `tunnel_id` matches `\d+(?:-\d+)+`)
- `r4tun/data/**`, `r4tun/references/**`
- `methods/plans/output/**`

All experiment outputs go under `logs/<run_id>/<tunnel>/r<ring>/`. If a runner
needs baseline files as input, COPY them into a `logs/...` sandbox first.
Restoring a parameter file does NOT restore overwritten data — these dirs are
never opened for writing in the first place.

Before running ANY runner that takes a `--base-dir`/`--output-dir` flag,
explicitly check the resolved value. If it falls under any prefix above, FIX
the default before running. The only legitimate writer of `data/<tunnel>/r*/**`
is `agents/1_preprocessing/scripts/run_all_rings.py` when the user explicitly
asks to regenerate the corpus.

## 3b) AGENTS-IMMUTABILITY (HARD RULE)

As of 2026-05-29, `agents/**` is FROZEN. Validation confirmed capability-
sufficiency: frozen preprocessing + searchable K/A/B offsets reaches near the
GT-derived ceiling (1-1/r18: ceiling 0.882, BO 0.823, regret 0.059;
`logs/aboffset_capability_v1/single_instance_gate.json`). Locked corpora:
`data/bo_calibration/` (6/6 ceiling pass) and `data/held-out/` (50/50 ceiling pass) —
read-only; never modify for BO trials or ablation — copy into `logs/<run_id>/` sandboxes only. Preprocessing QA:
3a intrinsic guardrails + 3b ceiling ≥ 0.85 (`agents/1_preprocessing/knowledge.md`,
`bo/lib/ceiling_gate.py`). Parameter/search changes only via
`bo/**` and `logs/**`. If a task needs an `agents/**` edit, STOP and ask.

## 4) Goal-Driven Execution

- Convert requests into verifiable success criteria.
- For multi-step work, use a short plan with explicit checks.
- Verify outcomes with tests/runs where appropriate before concluding.

## 5) Evidence Standards

- Do not stop at surface explanations.
- Back claims with evidence from run/query/output.
- If claiming causality, show controlled comparison (before/after or fixed/broken).
- If evidence contradicts a claim, drop the claim and re-investigate.

## 6) Communication Style

- Keep replies concise and actionable.
- Deliver one requested outcome at a time unless asked for more.

## 7) Project Rule Sources

Also apply focused rules in `.cursor/rules/`:

- `intrinsic-project.mdc`
- `experience-bank.mdc` — locked BO experience bank (`methods/paper/experience/`)